/**
 * OPENING, PLUS, MINUS, CLOSING — one entry per holding-window, keyed
 * `accountId|securityKey`.
 *
 * Read off the demat statements' own per-ISIN blocks: a printed opening
 * balance, every dated movement with its running balance, and a printed
 * closing balance. `opening + unitsIn - unitsOut + corporateAction` equals
 * `closing` on every entry carrying a split, because `motilalDemat.mjs`
 * refuses to publish a block whose rows do not walk its own two printed
 * balances — where they do not, every movement term is null and `reason`
 * says so rather than a zero claiming nothing moved.
 *
 * EVERY FIGURE IS A QUANTITY. A depository movement carries no price and no
 * counterparty, so none of these is a trade and `unitsIn`/`unitsOut` are
 * never called bought and sold. `encumbranceMoves` is a COUNT and in no
 * total: a pledge moves units between free and pledged without any leaving
 * the account, and summing one would report the holding twice.
 */
